  %% @mode architecture
  %% @subtitle LiteLLM is the authentication boundary; Xberg fetches remote documents only through an allowlisting proxy
  %% @card cyan | Request path | Clients call /mcp-rest/tools/call on LiteLLM, never Xberg directly | Only extract, detect_mime_type, get_version, and list_formats are exposed | Explicit injection phrases in tool results are redacted before return
  %% @card violet | Sandbox | Xberg has no route to the internal network or the Internet | Local paths and file:// URIs are disabled; only uploads and allowlisted URLs | In dev, extraction results can feed opt-in pgvector auto-indexing
  %% @card rose | Egress control | Squid allows HTTPS CONNECT to allowlisted hosts only and denies private ranges | xberg-dns answers NXDOMAIN for every unlisted name, so lookups cannot exfiltrate data | Keep the proxy, DNS, and Xberg allowlists aligned; grant MCP access only to trusted keys
  %% @tier 0: AG
  %% @tier 1: TR
